{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ae641e3b6f23683a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found tdd-workflow at `.claude/skills/ecc/tdd-workflow/SKILL.md`. Next, spawn the implementation sub-agent. Per the contract, the implementation agent must load tdd-workflow before coding. Include the following in the agent's prompt: TDD requirements (the main parts of the skill's workflow — RED first, GREEN, evidence) + the plan + exact task instructions.\n\nImplementation agent's prompt: describe the TDD discipline (RED: write a failing test first, run it and confirm it fails; GREEN: implement until it passes; keep a record of evidence), then pass the plan verbatim and the exact procedure. Also instruct: do not create .story-updates, do not commit noise, and report evidence (test output for RED, test output for GREEN, npm ls turbo, git log -1 --stat, git status).\n\nNote: per the plan, the implementer performs the commit (AC 4). After that, the reviewer reviews, and then I (the orchestrator) create the marker and execute phase 5's commit/push (phase 5's `git add .` commit — note: this is the orchestrator's marker commit, part of the completion protocol, and is permitted as coordination work).\n\nNow let's spawn the implementation agent.\n","signature":"05a7f74ff14f4eb491f627c6b19a2cb8"}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":114265,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b41b7cff-f541-40f9-ab74-f5dd04029f47","uuid":"08215578-3a5d-4b68-a351-f7c5a7747634","timestamp":"2026-08-20T08:10:46.113Z"}
