o not flag their absence from the commit, and do not review prd.json changes.\n\nKnown, pre-approved deviations from the plan (verify they are as described, don't re-litigate):\n1. Test run command uses explicit file path `node --test test/package.test.cjs` because `node --test test/` (directory form) fails with MODULE_NOT_FOUND on Node v22.23.2.\n2. The 2.x belt-and-suspenders regex in the test is `/\\^?2\\./` instead of the plan's self-contradictory `/^2\\./` (the plan's own mandated value '^2.5.0' starts with '^', so the plan's regex could never pass); the authoritative check is the exact-string assertion `pkg.devDependencies.turbo === '^2.5.0'`.\n\nVerify these acceptance criteria against the actual files (read them, don't trust my summary):\n- AC 1: package.json exists with name \"nextmove\", private true, workspaces array containing \"apps/*\".\n- AC 2: packageManager pinned to \"npm@10\", engines.node specifies 22.x.\n- AC 3: devDependencies pin turbo 2.x (specifier must resolve only within 2.x), scripts build/test/lint are exactly \"turbo run build\", \"turbo run test\", \"turbo run lint\".\n- AC 4: the 4 scaffold files are committed in commit 6cc5d66 with the scoped add — confirm `git show --stat 6cc5d66` lists exactly those 4 files and NO noise files (.last-branch, .ralph/, prd.json.bak, ralph.log, prd.json) leaked into the commit; confirm package-lock.json records turbo at a 2.x version; confirm .gitignore gained node_modules/ and nothing else.\n- Test mapping: test/package.test.cjs contains one test block per AC (AC 1–3 + JSON-parses precondition) and the assertions actually match the AC text (not weakened versions).\n\nAdditionally run the tests yourself to confirm green: `node --test test/package.test.cjs` — all 4 must pass.\n\nReturn the standard review output: findings (if any), then the Review Summary table with Verdict APPROVE / WARNING / BLOCK.","outputFile":"/tmp/claude-1001/-home-nitin-sharma-ralph-workspaces-6896163a-932b-4b96-bfe9-cdbb022c3538